<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<request-parameters>
<!--
  DRAFT -- validate with --dump before a real run. D16 = "Compressed
  Mortality, 1979-1998" (ICD-9 era). The icd9_chapter twin, one level finer:
    B_1  = D16.V1          (Year)
    B_2  = D16.V2-level2   (ICD Sub-Chapter -- ~70 groups, one level below
                            the ~17 Chapters)
    O_aar = aar_std + O_aar_enable = true   (age-adjusted; 2000 US std pop)

  WHY: sub-chapter grain lets a handful of specific rankable causes -- lung
  cancer, breast/prostate/colon cancer, stroke, diabetes, cirrhosis, COPD,
  the external causes -- extend a trend line back before 1999. It is NOT
  the NCHS "72 Selected Causes" list (WONDER's Compressed Mortality DBs
  don't expose that), so the frontend maps only the sub-chapters that line
  up 1:1 (or as a clean sum) with an ICD-10 113-list cause and leaves the
  rest at chapter grain. No comparability ratio is applied -- compare
  trends, not levels, across the 1979 / 1999 seams.

  Same CMF gotchas as icd9_chapter: O_aar=aar_std must accompany the
  checkbox; location V_ fields stay BLANK (CMF reads blank as all-US).
  {{YEAR_LIST}} -> V_D16.V1. Response cells: year, sub-chapter (label,
  h= depth), Deaths, Population, Crude Rate, Age-Adjusted Rate -> the same
  6-col contract as the `icd9` / `icd10` eras.

  Test: node --env-file=.env fetch.js --type=mortality --era=icd9_sub --years=1979-1981 --out=rows.json --dump
  On a 400: paste the <message> from pipeline/mortality_icd9_sub.raw.xml.
  THE DUMP MUST CONFIRM: V2-level2 is accepted as a Group By, the row
  shape is 6 cells, and the exact sub-chapter label strings (the frontend
  will map on those).
-->
